  "body": "The native post currently qualifies Berco Cut 0.25 mm wire. Add explicit Cobra Cut D 0.25 mm selections for a 40 mm cold die steel punch where the native control confirms the actual wire and requested quality.\n\nTwo synthetic offline jobs used a different quality name for each complete tuple. The job that selected Ra 0.30 made a main cut and three trims. The measured offsets were 0.250, 0.170, 0.145 and 0.135 mm. The job that selected Ra 0.70 made a main cut and two trims. The offsets were 0.245, 0.165 and 0.140 mm. These are measured motion values. An actual surface measurement requires a physical part.\n\nUse the effective rough offset for clearance. Set the wire at piece and work level. Refuse other stock heights, work types and mismatched recipes until qualified. Preserve the existing Berco conditions and the qualified 1 mm separation. Resolve the quality identity as tracked in #2984 before publishing this feature.\n\nSuggested labels are P6, effort:high, area:post, enhancement and source:agent.\n",
